{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Male and female He created them.</b> The soul and the intellect, for they are the essence in the study of wisdom, for the body counts for nothing but is an instrument for them." "<b>And He blessed them.</b> He blessed them with multiplication and increase of wisdom." "<b>And He called their name Adam.</b> For man is not called 'Adam' except by virtue of the soul and the intellect, for without them he is likened to the beasts that perish. And since he was in the image of Elohim, it was fitting for him to beget in his image and likeness, and so he did: for he begot the intellect and wisdom, which he designated in Shet — because the intellect (שכל) is the essence and foundation of all, from the expression אבן שתיה (the foundation stone), just as Shet was, in his generation, the essence of all descendants and the head of all the righteous." "<b>And further,</b> it appears proper to say: 'This is the book of the generations of Adam' — for the intent is upon Shet, whom he will mention in the section. And since of the two sons that he had, one was killed and the second was cursed and his line continued through Shet, he said of him, 'This is the book of the generations of Adam' — for he alone is his important progeny. And even though Scripture has already told, until now, many generations of Cain, they were not the generations of Adam but rather the generations of Chavah, compounded of the serpent — who is Samael — and they are Chanokh and Irad and Lemech. And from among them are those sealed with the name El, like the names of the angels: Mechuyael and Methushael. And concerning these generations of Cain Scripture said, 'The sons of HaElohim saw the daughters of men' — for they were sons of HaElohim, not sons of the first man. And on this the Rabbis of blessed memory darshaned: 'This is the book of the generations of Adam' — these are the generations of Adam, and the earlier ones are not generations of Adam. And what are they? Divinity (elohut)! For this reason he called them elohut, because all of them were born of Cain, who was born of Chavah through the power of El (a strange El). And understand this." "<b>And in the Midrash:</b> 'This is the book of the generations of Adam — on the day that Elohim created Adam' — this teaches you that as soon as Adam was created he established progeny. 'Male and female He created them, and He called their name Adam' — from this we learn that the woman too is called Adam, for she is included in the human species and has great essence, and so it is written explicitly: כתפארת אדם לשבת בית. And you should be roused to take to heart the expression 'male and female He created them,' for thus it is written: וייצר ה׳ אלהים, and it is written (I Chronicles 4:23): המה היוצרים — for the soul of the male is from the male and the soul of the female is from the female. And for this reason the serpent coupled with Chavah and not with Adam, because her soul is from the attribute that receives from the north, which is the left; and this you will find in Sefer haBahir at its end: 'The serpent said: since her soul is from the side of the north, I will soon entice her' — end of quote."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {3 "The reading כח אל נכר is translated hyper-literally; 'through the power of a strange El' — the phrase is textually difficult and may carry a Kabbalistic allusion left untranslated per rules."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:10:36.980042963Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}